    ],
    "equivalent": true,
    "why": "A leaving foot's leg reaches the foot itself rather than the ground under it: the difference is the foot's lift while its hold fades, over the first quarter of its flight, before it has risen far - on every slope pin, the stride sweeps and the random sessions it moves the hips 0.06 units at the most. It is kept because it is the leg's own reach (a rising foot is reached where it is), which the line's arriving half takes the other way: a foot coming down is reached at the ground it lands on."
  },
