    "why": "A standing foot lifted by its own stance's clock or by the stride's: every flight keeps to the stride's clock, so a foot strikes on it and the two agree to the frame's overshoot - the strikes' spacing, the hips through every reversal probe and the push's end move by 1.6 units at the most. The foot's own is kept so a stance's rocker and its end are read off one clock: the rocker's must be its own (GAIT-25), and a lift read off another could stand the foot on its toes past its push."
  },
